        "severity": "issue",
        "ok": true,
        "value": 0.65,
        "limit": 1.5,
        "meaning": "Carriage passes that knit and transfer nothing, for each pass that knits, from the end of the start to the piece's last row (128 movement-only, 198 knitting, 39 transfer passes). The carriage fetches one feeder at a time, so some are needed; many more than Kniterate's files means feeders are being shuffled, which costs time and is where issue #18's stops happened.",
        "kniterate": "The reversible front.kc is the busiest at 1.48; back.kc 0.98, sleeves.kc 0.94; every other reference file is at or under 0.49."
